      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Tic-Tac-Toe Board"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Since a tic-tac-toe board contains 9 squares, we will use an array of 9 elements to handle this task. And we will use the position number to identify a grid. For example, position 8 means the bottom middle grid."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Working of Tic-tac-toe in C++",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Two Players"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "As we have said, this game is played between two players."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In our game, the first player will always get the X symbol, and the second player will always get the O symbol."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Win and Draw Logic"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We will check the position of symbols for win/draw logic. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "if positions 4, 5, and 6 have the same X symbol, the first player won the game",
        "if positions 3, 5, and 7 have the same O symbol, the second player won the game",
        "if positions 2, 5, and 8 have the same X symbol, the first player won the game, and so on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "If all the positions are filled, but none of the players gets 3 of their symbols in a row, it's a draw."
    },
